.TH RETA 1 "2026-07-09" "reta arch mojo" "Reta commands"
.SH NAME
reta \- filter and render the Reta table
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reta
.RI [ main-options ]
.RI [ sub-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reta
is the public table command for Reta.  It selects rows, selects columns,
combines table domains and renders the result in a chosen output format.  The
program is intentionally parameter driven: main parameters start with one dash,
sub-parameters start with two dashes and must immediately follow the main
parameter to which they belong.
.PP
The most important rule is ordering.  A sub-parameter only belongs to the last
main parameter before it.  Inserting another main parameter in between changes
where the sub-parameter applies.
.SH MAIN PARAMETERS
.TP
.B -zeilen
Select rows.  Common sub-parameters are
.BR --alles ,
.BR --zeit= ,
.BR --zaehlung= ,
.BR --typ= ,
.BR --primzahlen= ,
.BR --vielfachevonzahlen= ,
.BR --primzahlvielfache= ,
.BR --vorhervonausschnitt= ,
.BR --vorhervonausschnittteiler ,
.BR --nachtraeglichneuabzaehlung= ,
.BR --nachtraeglichneuabzaehlungvielfache= ,
.BR --potenzenvonzahlen= ,
.BR --oberesmaximum=
and
.BR --invertieren .
.TP
.B -spalten
Select columns and column families.  Common sub-parameters are
.BR --alles ,
.BR --breite= ,
.BR --breiten= ,
.BR --wichtigsteverstehen= ,
.BR --menschliches= ,
.BR --planet= ,
.BR --religionen= ,
.BR --galaxie= ,
.BR --universum= ,
.BR --teilchen= ,
.BR --multiversum= ,
.BR --grundstrukturen= ,
.BR --groessenordnung= ,
.BR --primzahlwirkung= ,
.BR --wirtschaft= ,
.BR --procontra= ,
.BR --licht ,
.BR --bedeutung= ,
.BR --symbole ,
.BR --eigenschaften= ,
.BR --konzept2=
and
.BR --multiplikationen= .
.TP
.B -kombination
Select combination tables.  Important sub-parameters are
.B --galaxie=
and
.BR --universum= .
.TP
.B -ausgabe
Control rendering.  Common sub-parameters are
.BR --nocolor ,
.BR --art= ,
.BR --onetable ,
.BR --spaltenreihenfolgeundnurdiese= ,
.BR --keineleereninhalte ,
.BR --keineueberschriften
and
.BR --keinenummerierung .
.TP
.B -debug
Enable developer/debug behaviour.
.SH ROW EXPRESSIONS
Row expressions and numeric ranges can contain single numbers, comma lists,
ranges, distances, multiples and fractions.
.PP
Examples include
.BR 2 ,
.BR 3-5 ,
.BR 2,3-5 ,
.BR 5+2+4 ,
.BR v20-22 ,
.BR -20,v10 ,
.BR 1/2,3 ,
.B 1/2-3/3
and
.BR 4/5+2/2 .
.PP
.B --vorhervonausschnittteiler
adds divisors of the selected rows.  With multiples this can expand the result
substantially.
.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
.B -ausgabe --art=
accepts one output format.  The usual values are
.BR shell ,
.BR html ,
.BR csv ,
.B markdown
and
.BR bbcode .
.PP
.B --breite=0
uses the effective terminal width in the native path when available.
.SH LANGUAGE
Some frontends accept
.BR -language=english ,
.BR -language=deutsch
and additional language aliases.  Most table contents are historically German.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/reta
Default public executable for a standard installation.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/reta/libreta_core_mojo.so
Shared core library used by the thin
.B reta
starter.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/reta/csv
Installed CSV data.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/reta/assets
Installed generated catalogs, help text and static assets.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show the main help:
.PP
.nf
reta -h
.fi
.PP
Print rows 1 to 2 with the Sternpolygon religion columns as CSV:
.PP
.nf
reta -zeilen --vorhervonausschnitt=1-2 \\
     -spalten --religionen=sternpolygon --breite=40 \\
     -ausgabe --art=csv --nocolor
.fi
.PP
Render all columns as one HTML table:
.PP
.nf
reta -spalten --alles --breite=0 -ausgabe --art=html --onetable --nocolor
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rp (1),
.BR rpl (1),
.BR rpe (1),
.BR rpb (1),
.BR generate_html (1)
